# Normalize line endings to LF inside the repository.
#
# Without this, an editor saving CRLF produced whole-file diffs on files that
# had no content changes (yarn.lock alone churned ~3.6k lines). With
# `text=auto` git normalizes on commit and compares normalized content, so a
# CRLF working copy no longer shows up as a modified file.
* text=auto
